{"name":"Seafair Green","hex":"#b8f8d8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"}],"entries":[{"title":"Seafair","blocks":[{"text":"Seafair is an annual summer boating event, air show, and festival in Seattle, Washington, United States, that encompasses a wide variety of small neighborhood events leading up to several major citywide celebrations. Its main events include the Torchlight Parade, Seafair Cup hydroplane races, and an air show that often features the Blue Angels. Seafair also encompasses smaller block parties and local parades around the city and Seattle metropolitan area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Seafair2007.JPG/330px-Seafair2007.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seafair"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Naval_Air_Cadet_Choir_at_Aqua_Theatre%2C_August_2%2C_1954_-_DPLA_-_6b3b09aa6a540c446924cbdf16712885.jpg/500px-Naval_Air_Cadet_Choir_at_Aqua_Theatre%2C_August_2%2C_1954_-_DPLA_-_6b3b09aa6a540c446924cbdf16712885.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Naval_Air_Cadet_Choir_at_Aqua_Theatre%2C_August_2%2C_1954_-_DPLA_-_6b3b09aa6a540c446924cbdf16712885.jpg/1280px-Naval_Air_Cadet_Choir_at_Aqua_Theatre%2C_August_2%2C_1954_-_DPLA_-_6b3b09aa6a540c446924cbdf16712885.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Naval_Air_Cadet_Choir_at_Aqua_Theatre%2C_August_2%2C_1954_-_DPLA_-_6b3b09aa6a540c446924cbdf16712885.jpg/500px-Naval_Air_Cadet_Choir_at_Aqua_Theatre%2C_August_2%2C_1954_-_DPLA_-_6b3b09aa6a540c446924cbdf16712885.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Naval Air Cadet Choir performs at the Green Lake Aqua Theater for 1954 Seafair","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANaval_Air_Cadet_Choir_at_Aqua_Theatre%2C_August_2%2C_1954_-_DPLA_-_6b3b09aa6a540c446924cbdf16712885.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/2008_Seattle_Chinatown_Seafair_Parade_-_drill_team_stand_in_review_03.jpg/500px-2008_Seattle_Chinatown_Seafair_Parade_-_drill_team_stand_in_review_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=th